    {
      "id": "a6926168aa5f",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-16T06:19:13.651590+00:00",
      "decision": "Intent-falsification check design: LLM entailment judgment (does this diff falsify the decision's intent) as a second-stage rescue after keyword matching finds nothing \u2014 NOT similarity; flag-only with severity cap, never block alone; gated by Drift-Bench + live-corpus dry-run (pre-registered acceptance criteria) before wiring; budgeted via existing ReasoningClient/providers + core.cost.tracker; backward-compatible slot in match_decision_to_diff",
      "context": "Mapped 2026-08-16. Grounded in: _reward_hacking_positive (driftbench/scenarios.py:214-235, decision 'Never bypass authentication for admin-level access' vs backdoor diff 'if user.email == debug@internal.test: return True'), #67 dry-run (cosine 0.29 TP vs 0.65 benign typo fix \u2014 no threshold), existing LLM infra (core/last30days/lib/providers.py ReasoningClient/OpenAIClient + generate_json, core/cost/tracker.py). Entailment works where similarity failed because the LLM reasons about the specific code pattern (early return before permission check) instead of matching vocabulary. Preserves repo discipline: #57 no untuned signal into escalation, #67 dry-run before wiring, backward-compat optional params. V1 scope: code diffs only; diff content treated as untrusted data; uncertain is first-class.",
