  "goals": [
    {
      "id": "063021bb1eb3",
      "text": "Session-shape baselining (the drift-detection half). Tool-call counts, token counts, latency, output size, hang duration",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T20:50:01.432609+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-10T07:12:01.070368+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "5ad7ae94788e",
      "text": "Improve branding to match more precisely with the nature of the project.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:UX",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T20:51:38.058047+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-07T20:51:38.058047+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5efe8968745",
      "text": "Changing tagline to \"The Intention Engine\"",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:branding",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T20:59:22.527668+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-07T20:59:22.527668+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "43f95811bf29",
      "text": "Goal persistence / re-anchoring. Structure the prompt to re-anchor agent intent at each turn. Tropelex's Goals are purely passive: nothing re-injects an active goal back into a live agent's working context.",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "alignment",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T21:32:13.061383+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T02:51:40.523382+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8c978b3ae25",
      "text": "Coordination drift \u2014 decline in agreement between multiple agents over time, not just one agent's individual calibration. Nothing currently asks whether they're converging or diverging from each other. That's a real gap, not urgent, but worth remembering.",
      "status": "active",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "alignment",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T21:34:16.414004+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T21:12:43.665462+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a58ac59c62cc",
      "text": "\"Goal Drift\" (adherence score \u03b4(t) = 1 \u2212 A(t)) is conceptually what score_trend_drift does, just less formalized \u2014 we're comparing baseline-vs-recent risk/review-rate, not a proper adherence score against a goal. Worth knowing there's a more rigorous version of the same idea.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "alignment",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T21:36:12.590134+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-07T21:36:12.590134+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "7910c0002ebf",
      "text": "Revisit auto-wiring into record_session (the MCP end_session path \u2014 the higher-value integration point since it's what real agent sessions actually call) once it's clear whether agents populate summary with substantive enough text for scanning to have real yield.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:memory",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-08T03:28:29.109090+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-08T03:28:29.109090+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "b91dce7bdfa9",
      "text": "Review all dictionaries to assess whether or not they provide sufficient coverage. Create a .gitignored dictionary file that contains all of dictionaries with a description of the purpose and what it is connected to.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "robustness",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-08T03:34:54.780453+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-08T03:34:54.780453+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "195c358c1581",
      "text": "Draft Policy Schema for Gates",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "governance",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-08T07:15:55.131469+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T02:28:33.162235+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c8606d03b7c",
      "text": "Prevention report detailing what Tropelex has prevented so far or within a date range.",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "high",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-09T06:34:20.533458+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-09T15:30:42.302796+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "9ed5c10a1bf3",
      "text": "Friction persistence + keep/dismiss + auto ingestion from all coding tools.",
      "status": "active",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-09T06:37:08.926967+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-09T15:30:49.962285+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a4fbbbcfaba",
      "text": "Context Injection Middleware pattern with an MCP or a HTTP/LSP Proxy \n[ Any MCP-Enabled IDE ] \n       \u2502  \u25b2  (Standard JSON-RPC over Stdio)\n       \u25bc  \u2502\n[ Tropelex MCP Server ] \u2500\u2500> [ Context Rewriter ] \u2500\u2500> [ Gateway Router ]",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-10T06:16:12.812254+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-10T06:16:12.812254+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "38b3f97427e8",
      "text": "Add video explainers to the project, covering key features at a minimum.",
      "status": "active",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "nonsafety:documentation",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-10T22:38:36.976210+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T05:02:30.495972+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "9bdcfd3ffbb3",
      "text": "Add a visual faq to the project.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "nonsafety:documentation",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-10T22:39:37.744074+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-10T22:39:37.744074+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff57055a60de",
      "text": "Constitutional layer",
      "status": "active",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "alignment",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-10T23:49:04.947626+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-18T07:48:19.502928+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6363d5307e1",
      "text": "Soft enforcement + override-as-decision pattern (everywhere)",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "robustness",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:49:04.389559+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:49:04.389559+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e459bc93719a",
      "text": "Expand Drift-Bench into a continuous safety regression suite",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:49:38.224109+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:49:38.224109+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "ad6d0813134c",
      "text": "Goal re-anchoring + outer-alignment loop",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "alignment",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:50:06.488720+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:50:06.488720+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab2465f89d38",
      "text": "Handoff completeness as a first-class policy",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:51:04.171881+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T02:51:40.580236+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d3014ea2892",
      "text": "Close the biggest measured gap: reward-hacking / intent-preserving detectors",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "robustness",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:52:04.096724+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:52:04.096724+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "12e9f7a400f2",
      "text": "Promote the remaining safety logic still living in server.py fully into core/safety/ (and a thin core/governance/ if needed).",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:52:51.648912+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:52:51.648912+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "df455ea74871",
      "text": "Make Injection Sentinel patterns expandable from a project-level config rather than a hard-coded list.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "robustness",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:53:23.883953+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:53:23.883953+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4be6193737d",
      "text": "Correlate Session-Shape anomalies with later Ghost / Friction / Market outcomes so the system learns which behavioral signatures actually predict objective drift.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:53:53.354123+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:53:53.354123+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c2e2cbe953b",
      "text": "Add a simple \u201csafety budget\u201d per agent/session (cumulative risk score of actions taken) that can trigger review once exceeded.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-11T00:54:22.894008+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-11T00:54:22.894008+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "8de40234f900",
      "text": "#19 \u2014 Session Replay with AI Analysis",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-13T05:04:42.297555+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T18:03:21.155480+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "93c246a4dd80",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P0: Audit + relocate persona-market escalation off the GET path (gap D) \u2014 currently mutates safety_metadata with zero audit trail from a read endpoint",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "high",
      "category": "governance",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:11.088574+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T14:06:48.976853+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e2b205d5ff6",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P1: Instance auth (shared secret) + Host header validation on all write/mutating paths (gap A) \u2014 zero authentication today, directly validated by the real OpenRouter key-leak incident (2026-08-16)",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "critical",
      "category": "adversarial",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:12.931074+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T14:21:33.542535+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e21a15607a0e",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P2: Decision-level tamper-evidence via audit-snapshot hashing (gap B) \u2014 makes SAFETY.md's \"immutable decision history\" claim literally true, reuses core/audit.py's compute_hash",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "high",
      "category": "governance",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:14.752430+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T14:33:38.795359+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e54c5586a8f3",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P3: Intent-falsification LLM entailment check for ghost detection (gap C) \u2014 deferred: defends against a compromised/adversarial agent threat model that doesn't match current solo-operator usage; revisit when other operators' agents touch this instance",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "adversarial",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:16.599975+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:16.599975+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "9144ca7b9ce2",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P4: Wire real diffs into ghost detection \u2014 GET /ghost-decisions and the scheduler's post-hoc scan are structurally inert (diff_data hardcoded empty) despite being an already-shipped feature",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "robustness",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:18.525571+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-17T02:23:21.363200+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e99dac7ca592",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P5: Session cumulative safety budget + soft gate \u2014 joins existing signals (overrides, gate verdicts, risk, injection flags, friction, session-shape) into a per-session score; deferred, most valuable once sessions aren't personally supervised",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:20.347709+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:20.347709+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "703652bfd34e",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P6: Memory-poisoning anomaly/campaign detector \u2014 deferred: explicitly a multi-actor threat model (flag clusters, provenance spikes across many decisions) with no realistic campaign actor in current usage; cheaper than P3 if revisited early",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "low",
      "category": "adversarial",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:22.193566+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:22.193566+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "39e634b8bdfa",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P7: Extend injection screening coverage beyond decision text/context \u2014 goals, session summaries, preferences, alignment_considerations currently unscreened by core/injection_sentinel.py",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "adversarial",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:25.229490+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-17T02:42:13.324442+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "aed485c2b25a",
      "text": "Adversarial Hardening P8: Schedule Agent Surface Audit \u2014 core/agent_audit/scanner.py exists and works but runs manual-only; config/credential drift between runs goes undetected, directly relevant given the real OpenRouter key-leak incident (2026-08-16)",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "monitoring",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T13:39:27.212375+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-17T02:49:22.255892+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a90643cf1f3c",
      "text": "Write a vision.md document, containing the organism metaphor.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:documentation",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-17T22:39:03.713106+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-17T22:39:03.713106+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a071bedc9e6d",
      "text": "Create a repo search to find similar repos/projects to study.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": null,
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-18T08:33:03.148414+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-18T08:33:03.148414+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "43ba38dea880",
      "text": "Harden Tropelex against adversarial actors: authenticate all write paths, make decision history truly tamper-evident, and close the evasive-detection blind spot",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "high",
      "category": "adversarial",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-16T06:14:12.271697+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-19T21:28:03.202131+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "c62928802051",
      "text": "\"Add Citation\", \"Exclude\", and \"Scan Item\" buttons to repo seek and allow for a deeper search into similar repos. Also add export option for each search batch and all search batches, as well as persistent exclusions.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:research",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-20T02:13:01.470493+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-20T02:13:01.470493+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "f19eb244f8cf",
      "text": "Update markdown and other relevant docs in the repo.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:documentation",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-20T04:05:48.024832+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-20T04:05:48.024832+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "0f8268c4b1b6",
      "text": "#85 Adaptive Feed Scheduling & Query Rewriting \u2014 closes the loop on #9's existing novelty/anomaly signals (already computed, just not acted on): lengthen a feed's interval on repeated low-novelty runs, shorten it on anomaly spikes.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-24T23:27:20.058573+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-24T23:27:20.058573+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "796463c59479",
      "text": "#86 Multi-Project / Shared Feeds \u2014 lets a feed be global/opt-in across projects instead of siloed to one. Straightforward data-model + endpoint addition.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-24T23:27:49.213831+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-24T23:27:49.213831+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "17585ed92bc4",
      "text": "#88 Research Source Coverage Dashboard \u2014 cheaper than the wishlist entry implies: FeedRun.source_breakdown (per-source citation counts) is already computed by the scheduler and just never surfaced, and Citation.access_count already exists as a real \"did this citation get used\" signal \u2014 so \"which sources pull their weight\" is mostly aggregation over data that already exists, not new instrumentation.",
      "status": "proposed",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "general",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-24T23:29:05.285938+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-24T23:29:05.285938+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e1f74a2a2f2",
      "text": "Update the content and styling for the help/guide page.",
      "status": "achieved",
      "priority": "medium",
      "category": "nonsafety:documentation",
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-25T02:55:48.800361+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-25T02:58:25.349970+00:00"
    }
  ],
